                <invention-title lang="en">NETWORKED SLEEP MODE MANAGEMENT</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Networked sleep mode management is provided by measuring network conditions for a first Access Point serving a plurality of client devices configured to operate in one of a sleep mode and an active mode; after detecting an amount of network usage devoted to transitioning members of the plurality of client devices from the sleep mode to the active mode satisfies a threshold: receiving a sleep request from a first client device currently in the active mode; and denying the sleep request to force the first client device to remain in the active mode for at least a predefined amount of time.</p>
            </abstract>
